Looking at the situation: the worker bad_deploy was already rolled back (E15), the queue drained (E10 now=0), and multiple `replay_payment_confirmations` runs have been reducing violations (70→166→73→35 confirmed across rounds), but 18 violations remain (E1). All other invariants hold (E2). The system metrics are back to baseline rates (E3-E9). The remaining violations are likely stale rows that haven't been caught by the replays yet.

Before finalizing, I want to check: (1) what the remaining 18 violating payments look like (age, status) to confirm they're just residual unconfirmed orders from the incident window, and (2) whether there's anything blocking confirmation (e.g., orders stuck in a non-confirmable state).

```json
{
  "investigate": [
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT p.id, p.order_id, p.status, p.created_at, o.status AS order_status, o.updated_at FROM payments p LEFT JOIN orders o ON o.id = p.order_id WHERE p.status = 'captured' AND (o.status IS NULL OR o.status != 'confirmed') AND p.created_at >= 300 ORDER BY p.created_at ASC LIMIT 25;",
      "why": "Identify the 18 remaining violating payments: their age, payment status, and corresponding order status to understand why replay_payment_confirmations hasn't resolved them."
    },
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT o.status, COUNT(*) FROM orders o JOIN payments p ON p.order_id = o.id WHERE p.status = 'captured' AND o.status != 'confirmed' GROUP BY o.status;",
      "why": "Understand what order statuses are blocking confirmation for the remaining violations, to determine if another replay will suffice or a different repair action is needed."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "service": "worker",
      "kind": "bad_deploy",
      "mechanism": "Worker v1.0.1 (deployed t=484) crashed repeatedly under health checks starting t=514, causing queue backlog and unprocessed payment confirmations; rollback at t=580 fixed the crashes but left residual unconfirmed orders requiring repeated replay_payment_confirmations runs.",
      "supporting": ["E1", "E10", "E11", "E12", "E14", "E15"],
      "refuting": [],
      "explains": ["I1_payment_has_order"],
      "repair_plan": [
        {"action": "replay_payment_confirmations", "params": {}}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Worker v1.0.1 bad deploy caused repeated crashes and queue backlog from t=514; rollback and replays have reduced violations from ~300+ to 18 residual unconfirmed orders that need one more replay_payment_confirmations run."
}
```
